WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
- All right, it's a whole Barbie hour.

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:02.820
So, let's finish up

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.860
with something that
celebrates the iconic toy.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.848
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:08.910
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.370
He says playing with
dolls is just for kiddos.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.203
A Maryland woman

00:00:12.203 --> 00:00:14.310
recently discovered her
passion for Barbies.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.050
And she's blowing up social media

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:19.080
with videos of what she
calls Mini Meynelle.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.170
In the clips, you can see Mini
Meynelle doing everyday tasks

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.700
like figuring out what to wear

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.760
from her exclusive and
extensive mini-closet

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.740
or winding down after a long day.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.500
Her videos have racked
up millions of views.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.480
We have her on the line
right now to tell us more.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.680
Let's say hi to Meynelle,

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.779
watching on NBC Washington.
(audience cheering)

00:00:37.779 --> 00:00:38.820
Hi, Meynelle.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.580
So, you say dolls are kind
of new in your life, right?

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.210
- Yeah, so growing up,
I never really saw dolls

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.370
that really looked like me

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:50.820
or really represented me for who I was.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.260
So, it wasn't until recently

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.180
where I saw dolls on the
shelves diversify a little more.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.550
And that's when I started collecting.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:03.390
I started building more sets for them.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:06.510
And I started to collect more things.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:09.090
The pandemic also aided in that,

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:12.330
because it reignited my love for crafting.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:16.320
And that, coupled with my
newfound love for dolls,

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.870
helped me form what my TikTok is today.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:22.050
I would collect miniature
items for my mini me,

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.630
like food and furniture.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:27.600
And yeah, I wanted her to
really reflect who I was.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.610
- I love crafting as well.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.350
So, you've developed
serious skills though,

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.700
in the videos and in crafting.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.580
So, what have you learned
and what's next for you?

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.420
- Well, most of what I have
learned, it's a bit self-taught.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.140
For example, I started doing
stop-motion in my videos.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.910
I would take my mini me,

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.010
I'd move her, take another picture,

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.840
move her, snap another picture,

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.970
and it'd be that repetitive process

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:54.870
until I made a cute
little movie or a video.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:59.400
I also started making
doll houses and doll rooms

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.812
for my mini me.

00:02:00.812 --> 00:02:04.500
Something new that I
would love to get into

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.040
for my doll and I is traveling more.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.290
I definitely wanna travel with her more.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.780
I wanna take pictures with her out more.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.230
I've been to DC and I've
been to New York with her.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:19.290
But I would really love
to take her to the beach.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.700
- Oh, my gosh, I love this.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.470
And by the way, my kids are obsessed

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.030
with watching the stop-motion stuff,

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:25.950
like they would love this.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.870
And also, my kids love dolls.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.400
So, thanks so much, Meynelle.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.960
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.772
I hope you get to the beach.

00:02:32.772 --> 00:02:34.410
(audience cheering)
And that's not all, ma'am.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.090
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.830
makers of Friction, the go to erasable pen

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:38.820
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.250
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:42.480
just like yourself, ma'am.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.310
So, to get you to the
beach and to help you out,

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.810
they're gonna give you $1,000.

00:02:47.505 --> 00:02:49.270
- Thank you.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.290
- It was lovely to meet you, Meynelle.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.570
Thank you so much to all
of our guests this hour.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.393
Margot Robbie, Hilary Clinton,

00:02:56.393 --> 00:02:58.590
America Ferrera, and Lawrence Aaron.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:02:59.423
Y'all have a great day.

00:02:59.423 --> 00:03:02.670
And if it's not, try and change it.

